What happens between typing a URL and seeing the page?
URL: The browser reads the URL entered by the user.
DNS Lookup: DNS converts the domain name into an IP address.
Connection: The browser connects to the server using TCP and, for HTTPS, TLS.
HTTP Request: The browser sends an HTTP request to the server.
Server Response: The server sends back HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and other resources.
HTML Parsing: The browser converts HTML into the DOM.
CSS Parsing: The browser reads CSS and creates the CSSOM.
JavaScript Execution: JavaScript code runs and can change the webpage.
Rendering: The browser calculates layout, paints the elements, and displays the webpage.
